ening, and it has been lumpy (year-to-year swings of 25%).","At current returns, reinvesting 15% of profits supports about 2.2% a year of fundamental growth, too little to drive meaningful growth.","Free cash flow has compounded -10.3% a year over five years, short of the 5% durability bar.","Capex runs 1.7x depreciation (5.8% of sales), so it is building capacity for future growth.","Its Rule of 40 score is -0, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business.","It has beaten earnings estimates by 40.5% on average."],"own":["Insiders hold little stock (0.2%), and reported institutional holdings exceed 100% of shares (a sign of heavy share lending).","It returns 6.0% a year to shareholders (6.0% in buybacks).","The share count has shrunk 3.6% a year over five years, steadily raising each holder's stake."],"people":["With about 150,000 employees, each generates about $129K of revenue, 0.3x the Consumer Defensive median, and revenue has grown 8.3% a year across its filed history.","That works out to $7K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $5.3M (41x revenue per employee)."]},"profile":{"v":"WATCH","conv":52,"head":"Watch: priced 27% above its $109 fair value, but that value is low-confidence and the price is inside its $82.92\u2013$145 range.","pros":["Composite 40, above the 39 line (gates 11/25)","Net debt/EBITDA 0.7x","Piotroski F-score 8/9","Altman Z in the safe zone","12-1 month momentum +27%"],"cons":["Trades 27% above fair value of $109","Revenue shrank 5.3%/yr over 5y","EV/EBITDA 13.2x vs sector 10.0x","P/FCF 24.5x vs sector 15.4x","Heavy insider selling ($248.7M net over 12 months)"],"flags":[],"need":["no margin of safety","too few checks pass (conviction 52)"],"buy_below":92.4,"vc":{"base":108.71,"base_src":"dcf","bear":82.92,"bull":145.47,"alt_median":66.53,"n_alt":2,"gap":0.6339,"dispersion":0.3441,"level":"LOW","why":["models disagree (34% dispersion)","DCF is 63% above the other models' median ($66.53)"]},"med":{"pe":17.5447,"ev_ebitda":10.0,"